Below is the decomposition of the mission description into a hierarchical goal model with associated tasks. The model uses a tree structure where every non‐leaf goal has a runtime annotation (using “;” for sequential execution, “#” for parallel execution, or FALLBACK(… ) for alternative plans) and every leaf goal uses “–”. Goals are classified as either Achieve (bringing about a target world state), Perform (specifying activities to be executed), or Query (retrieving information). In this design, the main mission is an Achieve goal, while its sub‐goals (and the fallback alternatives) are treated as Perform goals.

──────────────────────────────
1. GOAL TABLE
──────────────────────────────

| Name       | Title                           | Text                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | Runtime                                       | Goal Type  | Target Condition or Enquired Information                                                                                              | Relation |
|------------|---------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|
| G1         | Execute Resource Mission        | Execute the mission of collecting required resources from storage and delivering them to the specified location. (Note: When multiple items are required from different storages, multiple robots may be assigned in parallel.)             | ; (sequential execution of Collection & Delivery phases) | Achieve   | All required resources have been collected from storage and delivered to the specified location.                                         | AND      |
| G2         | Collection Phase                | Navigate to storage, request the resource, and wait for retrieval. In case the battery falls below 10%, handle the situation by recharging and reassigning the mission.                                                                | FALLBACK((Plan Route ; Request Resource ; Wait for Retrieval), (Battery Low Handling)) | Achieve   | All requested resources are retrieved from the storage.                                                                              | AND      |
| G3         | Delivery Phase                  | Deliver the retrieved resources to the specified location. In case the battery falls below 30%, handle the situation by returning the resource to a checkpoint and reassigning the remaining task; if returning fails, trigger an alert. | FALLBACK((Deliver Runs), (Battery Low Handling)) | Achieve   | All resources are delivered to the specified location.                                                                               | AND      |
| G2.1       | Plan Route                       | Plan the optimal route to the storage based on waiting time and path distance.                                                                                                     | –                                             | Perform    | –                                                                                                                                      | AND      |
| G2.2       | Request Resource                 | Send a message to the storage with the precise specification of the requested resources.                                                                                         | –                                             | Perform    | –                                                                                                                                      | AND      |
| G2.3       | Wait for Retrieval               | Wait until the storage retrieves the requested resources.                                                                                                                        | –                                             | Perform    | –                                                                                                                                      | AND      |
| G2.4       | Battery Low Handling (Collection)| If the battery falls below 10%, navigate to the recharging station and reassign the mission to another robot.                                                                    | –                                             | Perform    | –                                                                                                                                      | AND      |
| G3.1       | Deliver Runs                     | Execute the delivery runs to transport all resources to the specified location.                                                                                                  | ; (sequential: Navigate then Deliver)         | Perform    | –                                                                                                                                      | AND      |
| G3.2       | Battery Low Handling (Delivery)  | If the battery falls below 30% during delivery, navigate to a checkpoint and reassign the remaining task to another robot; if returning fails, trigger an alert.                  | FALLBACK((Navigate to Checkpoint ; Reassign Remaining Task), (Trigger Alert)) | Perform    | –                                                                                                                                      | AND      |

